## Role-Based Access Control

| Role | Lands On | Can Access | Cannot Access |
|------|----------|-----------|--------------|
| `NIC_ADMIN` | `/dashboard` | Everything | — |
| `DEPT_CISO` | `/dept-dashboard` | Own dept findings, evidence, assets, tasks, intelligence | Global heatmap, other orgs |
| `DEPT_SECURITY` | `/dept-dashboard` | Own dept findings, upload evidence, assets, tasks | Dashboard, organizations |
| `VENDOR_ADMIN` | `/audit-dashboard` | Assigned audits, submit findings, validate evidence | Dept data, ledger |
| `AUDITOR` | `/audit-dashboard` | Assigned audit findings, validate evidence, tasks | Dept data, ledger |
| `REVIEWER` | `/review-dashboard` | Read-only findings, ledger, vendor scores, intelligence | Cannot modify anything |
| `OBSERVER` | `/review-dashboard` | Read-only findings only | Everything else |

**Enforcement is three-layered:**
1. **Next.js Middleware** — cookie checked server-side before any page renders
2. **NestJS Guards** — JWT + `RolesGuard` + `OrgScopeGuard` on every endpoint
3. **PostgreSQL RLS** — `SET app.user_org_id` enforced at DB query level

---

## The 5-Step Audit Workflow (PRD §9)

```
STEP 1          STEP 2          STEP 3          STEP 4          STEP 5
──────────      ──────────      ──────────      ──────────      ──────────
AUDITOR         DEPT TEAM       DEPT TEAM       AUDITOR         NIC ADMIN
Submit          Fix the         Upload          Validate        Approve
Finding         issue           proof           evidence        closure

Finding →       OPEN →          IN_REM →        REMEDIATED →    VALIDATED →
created         ACKNOWLEDGED    EVIDENCE        PENDING_VAL     CLOSED
                                UPLOADED
```

Every transition is hash-chained in the immutable ledger.

