## Complete Setup Guide

### Step 1 — Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-org/ncagp.git
cd ncagp
```

### Step 2 — PostgreSQL Database Setup

**macOS:**
```bash
# Connect as superuser
psql -U $(whoami) -d postgres

# Inside psql
CREATE DATABASE ncagp;
CREATE USER ncagp_app WITH PASSWORD 'ChangeThis!123' CREATEDB;
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE ncagp TO ncagp_app;
\c ncagp
GRANT ALL ON SCHEMA public TO ncagp_app;
\q
```

**Windows (run as Administrator in PowerShell):**
```powershell
# Connect to PostgreSQL
psql -U postgres

# Inside psql
CREATE DATABASE ncagp;
CREATE USER ncagp_app WITH PASSWORD 'ChangeThis!123' CREATEDB;
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE ncagp TO ncagp_app;
\c ncagp
GRANT ALL ON SCHEMA public TO ncagp_app;
\q
```

### Step 3 — MinIO Object Store

```bash
# macOS / Windows (Docker required)
docker run -d \
  --name ncagp-minio \
  -p 9000:9000 \
  -p 9001:9001 \
  -e MINIO_ROOT_USER=minioadmin \
  -e MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=minioadmin \
  minio/minio server /data --console-address ":9001"
```

Then open **http://localhost:9001** → login with `minioadmin` / `minioadmin` → create a bucket named **`ncagp-evidence`**.

> **Start MinIO every session:** `docker start ncagp-minio`

### Step 4 — Generate RS256 JWT Keys

**macOS:**
```bash
mkdir -p keys
openssl genrsa -out keys/private.pem 4096
openssl rsa -in keys/private.pem -pubout -out keys/public.pem
cat keys/private.pem   # copy this into .env
cat keys/public.pem    # copy this into .env
```

**Windows (PowerShell):**
```powershell
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path keys
openssl genrsa -out keys/private.pem 4096
openssl rsa -in keys/private.pem -pubout -out keys/public.pem
Get-Content keys/private.pem   # copy into .env
Get-Content keys/public.pem    # copy into .env
```

### Step 5 — Backend Configuration

Create `backend/.env`:

```env
# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://ncagp_app:ChangeThis!123@localhost:5432/ncagp"

# ── JWT (paste full PEM, replace newlines with \n) ───────────────
JWT_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIIE...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----"
JWT_PUBLIC_KEY="-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\nMIIB...\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----"
JWT_EXPIRES_IN="8h"

# ── MinIO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
STORAGE_ENDPOINT="http://localhost:9000"
STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY="minioadmin"
STORAGE_SECRET_KEY="minioadmin"
STORAGE_BUCKET="ncagp-evidence"

# ── Optional: SLA Email Alerts ────────────────────────────────────
# Generate app password at: myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
SMTP_USER="your.email@gmail.com"
SMTP_PASS="your-16-char-app-password"

# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
FRONTEND_URL="http://localhost:3001"
```

> **Windows tip:** Use `notepad backend\.env` or VS Code to create the file.

**Paste the PEM keys correctly** — replace every literal newline with `\n`:

**macOS:**
```bash
# Auto-format keys for .env
PRIVATE=$(cat keys/private.pem | awk '{printf "%s\\n", $0}')
PUBLIC=$(cat keys/public.pem | awk '{printf "%s\\n", $0}')
echo "JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=\"$PRIVATE\""
echo "JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=\"$PUBLIC\""
```

**Windows (PowerShell):**
```powershell
$private = (Get-Content keys/private.pem -Raw) -replace "`r`n","\n" -replace "`n","\n"
$public  = (Get-Content keys/public.pem  -Raw) -replace "`r`n","\n" -replace "`n","\n"
Write-Output "JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=`"$private`""
Write-Output "JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=`"$public`""
```

### Step 6 — Backend Install & Migrate

```bash
cd backend

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Generate Prisma client
npx prisma generate

# Run migrations (creates all 15 tables)
npx prisma migrate dev --name init

# Apply security hardening (RLS + immutability triggers)
# macOS:
PGPASSWORD=ChangeThis!123 psql -U ncagp_app -d ncagp \
  -f prisma/migrations/001_security_hardening.sql

# Windows (PowerShell):
$env:PGPASSWORD="ChangeThis!123"
psql -U ncagp_app -d ncagp -f prisma/migrations/001_security_hardening.sql

# Apply feature additions (API keys, MFA columns)
# macOS:
psql -U shreyanshtripathi -d ncagp -f prisma/migrations/002_features_fixed.sql

# Windows:
psql -U postgres -d ncagp -f prisma/migrations/002_features_fixed.sql

# Seed database (creates users + demo findings)
npx ts-node prisma/seed.ts

# Seed control library (30 ISO 27001 + NIST controls)
npx ts-node prisma/seed-controls.ts

# Start development server
npm run start:dev
```

Backend will print: `🛡️ NCAGP API running on: http://localhost:3000/api`

### Step 7 — Frontend Install & Run

```bash
cd frontend

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start development server
npm run dev
```

Frontend runs at: **http://localhost:3001**

### Step 8 — Verify the Setup

```bash
# macOS / Windows Git Bash / WSL
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"admin@nic.in","password":"Admin@1234!"}' \
  | python3 -c "import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin).get('accessToken','FAILED'))")

echo "Token acquired: ${TOKEN:0:30}..."

# Verify risk heatmap
curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/findings/risk-heatmap \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | python3 -m json.tool

# Verify ledger chain
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/ledger/verify-chain \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{}' | python3 -m json.tool
```

**Windows PowerShell:**
```powershell
$response = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login" `
  -Method POST -ContentType "application/json" `
  -Body '{"email":"admin@nic.in","password":"Admin@1234!"}'

$TOKEN = $response.accessToken
Write-Output "Token: $($TOKEN.Substring(0,30))..."

# Test heatmap
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:3000/api/findings/risk-heatmap" `
  -Headers @{Authorization="Bearer $TOKEN"} | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 5
```

